</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Intra-domain class imbalance.</span>
Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.1 Domain Gaps and Class Imbalances ‣ 5 Robustness of VFMs to Data Gaps ‣ Rethinking the Backbone in Class Imbalanced Federated Source Free Domain Adaptation: The Utility of Vision Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> illustrates that VFMs effectively mitigate the effects of imbalance. Here, Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.1 Domain Gaps and Class Imbalances ‣ 5 Robustness of VFMs to Data Gaps ‣ Rethinking the Backbone in Class Imbalanced Federated Source Free Domain Adaptation: The Utility of Vision Foundation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> compares two scenarios in TL setting.
The accuracy degradation after target adaptation between <span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">sbtb</span> (<sup id="S5.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">∗</span></sup>) and <span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">siti</span> (<sup id="S5.SS1.p3.1.5" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">†</span></sup>) is 4.4% for ResNet-50, 3.0% for ViT-S, and 2.9% for ViT-B.
These results indicate that VFMs experience less accuracy degradation compared to ResNet, highlighting their superior performance. It suggests that VFMs are more effective in addressing the impact of data imbalance during source training and target
adaptation. Consequently, ViTs can manage intra-domain class imbalance more efficiently.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T3.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S5.T3.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The scenarios of <span id="S5.T3.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">sbtb</span> and <span id="S5.T3.10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">siti</span> under TL setting. The difference of target accuracy between <span id="S5.T3.10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">sbtb</span> (<sup id="S5.T3.10.4" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S5.T3.10.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">∗</span></sup>) and <span id="S5.T3.10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">siti</span> (<sup id="S5.T3.10.6" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S5.T3.10.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">†</span></sup>) (Target diff.) is shown. Three domains and nine runs for each domain are averaged.</span></figcaption>
<div id="S5.T3.11" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:223.6pt;height:74.4pt;vertical-align:-35.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-37.3pt,12.4pt) scale(0.8,0.8) ;">
